This is a prospective diagnostic plan only. No implementation, timing, memory, profiling, candidate tuning or production change is authorized by this document. The wrapper study is already frozen at receipt bd84dc28fee7f1c3d90c68ad94b318afa73c54a18fb9f4bc098de61807b15bf9 and manifest7c36f6c5bc33187fe63c34f09a62121cbe4f7f7621b4da335feb283ffb855e18. Its small-standard +0.794159% change of medians, -0.516696% median paired change, all-percentile -7.874804% change with overlapping ranges, and positive single-p95 lifetime RSS are retained. The older positive all-percentile result remains public at commit455ab6c46461981e6e4331ba5612d5362bf4ad22. Neither sign proves a compiler or wrapper cause.

Three explanations remain open: ordinary host/GC/order variability; an imported module or changed entry layout affecting execution of otherwise identical bodies; and changes in dispatch/all-percentile call structure. Same-window source-controlled roles can narrow these explanations but cannot by themselves identify JIT internals. CPU/memory profiling is a separate future task and quiet authorization, not part of this plan.

The proposed primary diagnostic has five roles: authenticated original; exact production baseline9269cf...91371; frozen wrapper b3feba...aace0 plus helper de334c...bd58c; frozen mixed algorithm225a47...d53 plus the same helper; and a new import-only negative control. Import-only would add exactly the helper import to baseline without changing any reduction/registry/dispatch/transport body or calling the helper. Its inverse must reconstruct exact baseline bytes. It has not been implemented, hashed or accepted. It isolates the presence of the module graph better than comparing two entries that also change dispatch; module source length and layout still differ, so it is not a causal compiler proof. No disabled helper branch, runtime flags, timed instrumentation or modified helper is proposed.

Retain all seven prior workload definitions,14 exact input/expectation files, generator seeds and canonical output/cache graphs. Each role gets seven fresh-process repetitions. Fix a five-role rotating order before execution; the primary series is245 children. Run two independently authorized, completed windows rather than silently merging or choosing a favorable one. Both windows include all same-window controls. Preserve raw per-run signed candidate-minus-each-control deltas, ratio of medians, median paired percentages, min/max, overlaps, output/cache checks, failures and censoring separately for each window. Show cross-window baseline/original variation descriptively. Do not pool windows into a replacement147-child study or reinterpret the existing three-role results.

An optional separately frozen supplemental protocol would keep the same inputs/expectations but increase warmup/iteration counts for the four untouched-body controls smallStandard,largeStandard,allPercentiles,allCalculations. Proposed counts are16 warmups/64 measured calls, with seven repetitions and the same five roles (140children). This addresses the existing multi-selection two-warmup/three-call limitation prospectively. It is a separate observation block, never a substitute for the fixed primary inputs/cadence and never a retroactive correction to existing trials. A separate readiness must authenticate expected graphs and source-stable bounded startup/work before approving it. If any original workload would exceed the existing60s child budget, reject the proposed protocol before measurement; do not silently lower counts or raise a measured limit after a failure.

Before any execution, freeze both-module identities, all five role sources, actual original six loaded CJS files/two archive identities/Node, control ordering, seeds, source/body inverse proofs,14 inputs/expectations, lifecycle/capture bounds and complete cache/alias/null-mode contracts. Run the existing finite full/held-out/adversarial/cache comparison campaign plus new independent held-out corpora under a fixed new seed before asking for a quiet window. Retain every failed preparation/correctness attempt. Do not claim universal correctness from a finite corpus. Source inspection/body equality and private host routing are separate contracts; Node measurements do not establish browser or application host behavior.

Predeclared structural gates are exact immutable sources/inputs, a correctly reconstructed import-only control, all output/state/cache/alias contracts, source-before/after identity, complete role/repetition order, every failure visible, numeric-PID observer ownership where applicable, and exact signed/null arithmetic. Any source/selection/output failure invalidates that diagnostic block; partial raw observations remain. No numeric speed acceptance threshold is introduced. The diagnostic cannot select or integrate a candidate, even if its medians improve. A positive candidate/control median, overlapping ranges, inconsistent direction between windows, or positive resource diagnostic remains visible and prevents a universal nonregression/superiority claim. A future product acceptance proposal requires independent review and explicit authorization, not a best-case result from this plan.

If resource investigation is separately approved after timing diagnosis, use fresh one-implementation children with the same five roles (245children/window), keeping lifetime,100ms polled and checkpoint peaks distinct. Preserve all20 metrics, release baselines, retained graphs and shared serializer/cache-read pressure. Keep negative values and zero-control unavailable percentages.256MiB old-space and512MiB sampled RSS are not an instantaneous OS memory sandbox;120s child deadlines/numeric PID observation do not prove descendant/start identity, and the prior memory controller has no outer hard watchdog. Designing a new outer bound or stronger ownership check requires a separately frozen lifecycle contract before measurement.

Conservative scheduling proposals, not executable authorizations: primary timing8–12minutes per245-child window; optional supplemented timing12–20minutes per window after a correctness-only bounded work check; memory15–25minutes per245-child window. Root must independently accept a new readiness and separately authorize/close each fresh window. Other agents/root pause tests, builds, scans, writes, publication, browser and profiler work. Idle owned preview servers and uncontrolled Windows/user activity must remain disclosed. No machine isolation, causal attribution, full parity or performance acceptance is claimed.
